WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:06.410
Hypertext Transfer Protocol, HTTP, is the
main protocol used for webpages, such as the

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.600
one we see.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.841
With a heightened awareness of security in
data transfers, most webpages use the secure

00:00:12.841 --> 00:00:18.199
version of HTTP, HTTPS, as we see here.

00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:28.099
The difference between HTTP and HTTPS is simply
this: Data transmitted over HTTP is not encrypted.

00:00:28.099 --> 00:00:32.390
Data transmitted over HTTPS is encrypted.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:37.719
Any sensitive data transmitted over the internet
should be encrypted, and thus HTTPS should

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:39.059
always be used.

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:44.741
A protocol in the same realm as HTTP and HTTPS
is FTP, File Transfer Protocol.

00:00:44.741 --> 00:00:50.860
This protocol is often used to upload and
download files to and from a web server.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.129
For port numbers, HTTP transmits over port
80, HTTPS port 443, and FTP port 21.

